                <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>

                <h3>What is a good GPA in Pakistani universities?</h3>
                <p>A GPA of 3.5+ is considered very good. 3.0-3.49 is good, 2.5-2.99 is average, and below 2.5 needs improvement. Many scholarships require 3.0+ GPA.</p>

                <h3>How do I convert GPA to percentage in Pakistan?</h3>
                <p>Use the formula: <strong>Percentage = (GPA ÷ 4.0) × 100</strong>. For example, 3.5 GPA = (3.5 ÷ 4.0) × 100 = 87.5%.</p>

                <h3>What is the difference between GPA and CGPA?</h3>
                <p>GPA is calculated for a single semester, while CGPA (Cumulative GPA) is the overall average across all semesters completed.</p>

                <h3>Can I calculate GPA without credit hours?</h3>
                <p>No, credit hours are essential for calculating GPA. Each subject has a specific credit hour value that weights its contribution to your overall GPA.</p>

                <h3>How often should I check my GPA?</h3>
                <p>You should check your GPA at the end of every semester. This helps you track your academic progress and identify any areas that need improvement.</p>

